2026-05-25T10:32:58.602Z {"session_id":"89bec47a-fde9-463a-861e-f47ff075ce36","transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\yasmi\\.claude\\projects\\e--workstuff-platform-ai-assistant-worktrees-agents-architectural-review-project-files\\89bec47a-fde9-463a-861e-f47ff075ce36.jsonl","cwd":"e:\\workstuff\\platform_ai_assistant.worktrees\\agents-architectural-review-project-files","permission_mode":"default","effort":{"level":"high"},"hook_event_name":"PostToolUse","tool_name":"Read","tool_input":{"file_path":"e:\\workstuff\\platform_ai_assistant.worktrees\\agents-architectural-review-project-files\\app\\services\\prompt_builder.py","offset":460,"limit":60},"tool_response":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"e:\\workstuff\\platform_ai_assistant.worktrees\\agents-architectural-review-project-files\\app\\services\\prompt_builder.py","content":"\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Assemble the full static prompt per language\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef _build_static_prompt(lang: str) -> str:\n    if lang == \"kz\":\n        role = \"<role>\\nТы — официальный ИИ-ассистент платформы iSEL.\\nЯзык: казахский.\\n</role>\"\n        lang_rule = (\n            \"<language_rule>\\n\"\n            \"Язык пользователя: КАЗАХСКИЙ. Отвечай ИСКЛЮЧИТЕЛЬНО на казахском языке.\\n\"\n            \"Если <context> содержит русские инструкции — переведи их на казахский полностью перед ответом.\\n\"\n            \"КАТЕГОРИЧЕСКИ ЗАПРЕЩЕНО отвечать на русском языке.\\n\"\n            \"</language_rule>\"\n        )\n        rules = _RULES_KZ\n        formatting = _FORMATTING_KZ\n    else:\n        role = \"<role>\\nТы — официальный ИИ-ассистент платформы iSEL.\\nЯзык: русский.\\n</role>\"\n        lang_rule = (\n            \"<language_rule>\\n\"\n            \"Язык пользователя: РУССКИЙ. Отвечай на русском языке.\\n\"\n            \"</language_rule>\"\n        )\n        rules = _RULES_RU\n        formatting = _FORMATTING_RU\n\n    intent_handling = (\n        \"<intent_handling>\\n\"\n        + _build_intent_handling(lang)\n        + \"\\n</intent_handling>\"\n    )\n    nav_facts = (\n        \"<navigation_facts>\\n\"\n        + _build_nav_facts(lang)\n        + \"\\n</navigation_facts>\"\n    )\n\n    return \"\\n\\n\".join([role, lang_rule, intent_handling, nav_facts, rules, formatting])\n\n\n# Build once at module load — identical per language so OpenAI can cache them.\n_STATIC_RU: str = _build_static_prompt(\"ru\")\n_STATIC_KZ: str = _build_static_prompt(\"kz\")\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Public API\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef build_system_prompt(\n    language: str,\n    history: str,\n    intent: Optional[str],\n    entity: Optional[str],\n    current_step: Optional[int],\n    page: Optional[str],\n    situation: Optional[str] = None,\n) -> str:","numLines":60,"startLine":460,"totalLines":588}},"tool_use_id":"toolu_011pykveuDLxeughfF2XCTy9","duration_ms":3}

2026-05-25T10:32:58.728Z {"session_id":"89bec47a-fde9-463a-861e-f47ff075ce36","transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\yasmi\\.claude\\projects\\e--workstuff-platform-ai-assistant-worktrees-agents-architectural-review-project-files\\89bec47a-fde9-463a-861e-f47ff075ce36.jsonl","cwd":"e:\\workstuff\\platform_ai_assistant.worktrees\\agents-architectural-review-project-files","permission_mode":"default","effort":{"level":"high"},"hook_event_name":"PostToolUse","tool_name":"Read","tool_input":{"file_path":"e:\\workstuff\\platform_ai_assistant.worktrees\\agents-architectural-review-project-files\\app\\models\\schemas.py"},"tool_response":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"e:\\workstuff\\platform_ai_assistant.worktrees\\agents-architectural-review-project-files\\app\\models\\schemas.py","content":"from pydantic import BaseModel\nfrom typing import Optional\n\n\nclass ChatRequest(BaseModel):\n    message: str\n    session_id: str\n    page: Optional[str] = None\n    language: Optional[str] = \"ru\"\n\n\nclass ChatResponse(BaseModel):\n    answer: str\n    source: str\n    handoff: bool = False\n\n\nclass FlowState(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"Per-session flow state persisted in SessionManager.\"\"\"\n    intent: Optional[str] = None\n    entity: Optional[str] = None\n    step: Optional[int] = None       # linear flows (TU)\n    situation: Optional[str] = None  # scenario flows (Real Estate)\n    locked: bool = False             # True once a flow is underway\n    original_question: Optional[str] = None  # first user message that triggered this intent\n\n\n# Backward-compat alias — remove after all callers updated\nSessionState = FlowState\n","numLines":30,"startLine":1,"totalLines":30}},"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K3u5GpWi5TjJRo1mzVfj8W","duration_ms":3}

2026-05-25T10:33:06.117Z {"session_id":"89bec47a-fde9-463a-861e-f47ff075ce36","transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\yasmi\\.claude\\projects\\e--workstuff-platform-ai-assistant-worktrees-agents-architectural-review-project-files\\89bec47a-fde9-463a-861e-f47ff075ce36.jsonl","cwd":"e:\\workstuff\\platform_ai_assistant.worktrees\\agents-architectural-review-project-files","permission_mode":"default","effort":{"level":"high"},"hook_event_name":"PreToolUse","tool_name":"Read","tool_input":{"file_path":"e:\\workstuff\\platform_ai_assistant.worktrees\\agents-architectural-review-project-files\\app\\config\\service_registry.py"},"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SP9PJSia6Q1Y7FTaSi5Kbz"}

2026-05-25T10:33:06.572Z {"session_id":"89bec47a-fde9-463a-861e-f47ff075ce36","transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\yasmi\\.claude\\projects\\e--workstuff-platform-ai-assistant-worktrees-agents-architectural-review-project-files\\89bec47a-fde9-463a-861e-f47ff075ce36.jsonl","cwd":"e:\\workstuff\\platform_ai_assistant.worktrees\\agents-architectural-review-project-files","permission_mode":"default","effort":{"level":"high"},"hook_event_name":"PostToolUse","tool_name":"Read","tool_input":{"file_path":"e:\\workstuff\\platform_ai_assistant.worktrees\\agents-architectural-review-project-files\\app\\config\\service_registry.py"},"tool_response":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"e:\\workstuff\\platform_ai_assistant.worktrees\\agents-architectural-review-project-files\\app\\config\\service_registry.py","content":"\"\"\"ServiceRegistry — single interface for loading and querying service configs.\n\nLoads config/services.yaml and config/keywords.yaml once at startup (singleton).\nAll intent detection, keyword lookups, and flow-type queries go through here.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport re\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Optional\n\nimport yaml\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Data classes\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n@dataclass\nclass FlowConfig:\n    type: str                            # \"linear\" | \"scenario\" | \"faq\"\n    max_steps: Optional[int] = None\n    requires_entity: bool = False\n    scenarios: list[str] = field(default_factory=list)\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass ServiceConfig:\n    service_id: str\n    display_name: dict[str, str]         # {\"ru\": \"...\", \"kz\": \"...\"}\n    description: dict[str, str]\n    detection_patterns: dict[str, list[str]]  # {\"filename\": [...], \"content\": [...]}\n    flow: FlowConfig\n    navigation_path: dict[str, str]\n    entities: list[str] = field(default_factory=list)\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Registry (singleton)\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n_CONFIG_DIR = Path(__file__).parent.parent.parent / \"config\"\n\n\nclass ServiceRegistry:\n    \"\"\"Singleton that loads services.yaml + keywords.yaml once.\"\"\"\n\n    _instance: Optional[\"ServiceRegistry\"] = None\n\n    def __new__(cls) -> \"ServiceRegistry\":\n        if cls._instance is None:\n            instance = super().__new__(cls)\n            instance._services: dict[str, ServiceConfig] = {}\n            instance._flow_keywords: dict[str, dict[str, list[str]]] = {}\n            instance._filter_keywords: dict[str, dict[str, list[str]]] = {}\n            instance._load()\n            cls._instance = instance\n        return cls._instance\n\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n    # Loading\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n    def _load(self) -> None:\n        self._load_services()\n        self._load_keywords()\n\n    def _load_services(self) -> None:\n        path = _CONFIG_DIR / \"services.yaml\"\n        with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n            data = yaml.safe_load(f)\n\n        for service_id, svc in (data.get(\"services\") or {}).items():\n            flow_raw = svc.get(\"flow\") or {}\n            flow = FlowConfig(\n                type=flow_raw.get(\"type\", \"faq\"),\n                max_steps=flow_raw.get(\"max_steps\"),\n                requires_entity=flow_raw.get(\"requires_entity\", False),\n                scenarios=flow_raw.get(\"scenarios\") or [],\n            )\n            self._services[service_id] = ServiceConfig(\n                service_id=service_id,\n                display_name=svc.get(\"display_name\") or {},\n                description=svc.get(\"description\") or {},\n                detection_patterns=svc.get(\"detection_patterns\") or {},\n                flow=flow,\n                navigation_path=svc.get(\"navigation_path\") or {},\n                entities=svc.get(\"entities\") or [],\n            )\n\n    def _load_keywords(self) -> None:\n        path = _CONFIG_DIR / \"keywords.yaml\"\n        with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n            data = yaml.safe_load(f)\n\n        for service_id, kw in (data.get(\"keywords\") or {}).items():\n            self._flow_keywords[service_id] = kw.get(\"flow_keywords\") or {}\n            self._filter_keywords[service_id] = kw.get(\"filter_keywords\") or {}\n\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n    # Service queries\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n    def get_service(self, service_id: str) -> Optional[ServiceConfig]:\n        return self._services.get(service_id)\n\n    def list_services(self) -> dict[str, ServiceConfig]:\n        return dict(self._services)\n\n    def get_display_name(self, service_id: str, language: str = \"ru\") -> str:\n        svc = self._services.get(service_id)\n        if not svc:\n            return service_id\n        return svc.display_name.get(language) or svc.display_name.get(\"ru\") or service_id\n\n    def get_flow_type(self, service_id: str) -> str:\n        svc = self._services.get(service_id)\n        return svc.flow.type if svc else \"faq\"\n\n    def get_navigation_path(self, service_id: str, language: str = \"ru\") -> str:\n        svc = self._services.get(service_id)\n        if not svc:\n            return \"\"\n        return svc.navigation_path.get(language) or svc.navigation_path.get(\"ru\") or \"\"\n\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n    # Keyword queries\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n    def get_flow_keywords(self, service_id: str, language: str) -> list[str]:\n        \"\"\"Keywords used for intent classification and FAQ-interruption gate.\"\"\"\n        return list(self._flow_keywords.get(service_id, {}).get(language) or [])\n\n    def get_all_flow_keywords(self, service_id: str) -> list[str]:\n        \"\"\"Combined RU + KZ flow keywords for a service.\"\"\"\n        kw = self._flow_keywords.get(service_id) or {}\n        return list(kw.get(\"ru\") or []) + list(kw.get(\"kz\") or [])\n\n    def get_filter_keywords(self, service_id: str) -> list[str]:\n        \"\"\"Filter keywords from keywords.yaml (retained for reference/tooling).\"\"\"\n        kw = self._filter_keywords.get(service_id) or {}\n        return list(kw.get(\"ru\") or []) + list(kw.get(\"kz\") or [])\n\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n    # Intent detection (replaces _slug_intent in ingestion/ingest.py)\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n    def detect_intent(self, text: str, filename: str = \"\") -> Optional[str]:\n        \"\"\"Detect service intent from document text and/or filename.\n\n        Checks filename patterns first (more reliable), then content patterns.\n        Returns the matching service_id, or None if nothing matches.\n\n        Space-pads the combined string so patterns like ' ту ' don't match\n        inside longer words.\n        \"\"\"\n        combined = \" \" + ((text or \"\") + \" \" + (filename or \"\")).lower() + \" \"\n\n        for service_id, svc in self._services.items():\n            patterns = svc.detection_patterns\n\n            for pat in patterns.get(\"filename\") or []:\n                if pat.lower() in \" \" + filename.lower() + \" \":\n                    return service_id\n\n            for pat in patterns.get(\"content\") or []:\n                if pat.lower() in combined:\n                    return service_id\n\n        return None\n\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n    # Intent classification helpers (used by flows/registry.py)\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n    def build_intent_keywords_map(self) -> dict[str, list[str]]:\n        \"\"\"Return {service_id: [all ru+kz flow keywords]} for all services.\n\n        Used by flows/registry.py to rebuild INTENT_KEYWORDS from config\n        instead of maintaining a separate hardcoded dict.\n        \"\"\"\n        return {sid: self.get_all_flow_keywords(sid) for sid in self._services}\n\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n    # Page-intent map (static, can be extended to YAML later)\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n    _PAGE_INTENT_MAP: dict[str, list[str]] = {\n        \"tu_application\": [\n            \"технических условий\", \"техусловия\",\n            \"шаг 1\", \"шаг 2\", \"шаг 3\", \"шаг 4\", \"шаг 5\",\n        ],\n        \"real_estate\": [\n            \"объект недвижимости\", \"объекты недвижимости\",\n            \"добавление объекта\",\n        ],\n    }\n\n    def detect_intent_from_page(self, page: str) -> Optional[str]:\n        lower = page.lower()\n        for service_id, keywords in self._PAGE_INTENT_MAP.items():\n            if any(kw in lower for kw in keywords):\n                return service_id\n        return None\n","numLines":206,"startLine":1,"totalLines":206}},"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SP9PJSia6Q1Y7FTaSi5Kbz","duration_ms":1}

2026-05-25T10:33:06.596Z {"session_id":"89bec47a-fde9-463a-861e-f47ff075ce36","transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\yasmi\\.claude\\projects\\e--workstuff-platform-ai-assistant-worktrees-agents-architectural-review-project-files\\89bec47a-fde9-463a-861e-f47ff075ce36.jsonl","cwd":"e:\\workstuff\\platform_ai_assistant.worktrees\\agents-architectural-review-project-files","permission_mode":"default","effort":{"level":"high"},"hook_event_name":"PreToolUse","tool_name":"Read","tool_input":{"file_path":"e:\\workstuff\\platform_ai_assistant.worktrees\\agents-architectural-review-project-files\\app\\services\\llm_service.py"},"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VSAF5bg2WE1PVLNFNmpDna"}

2026-05-25T10:33:07.013Z {"session_id":"89bec47a-fde9-463a-861e-f47ff075ce36","transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\yasmi\\.claude\\projects\\e--workstuff-platform-ai-assistant-worktrees-agents-architectural-review-project-files\\89bec47a-fde9-463a-861e-f47ff075ce36.jsonl","cwd":"e:\\workstuff\\platform_ai_assistant.worktrees\\agents-architectural-review-project-files","permission_mode":"default","effort":{"level":"high"},"hook_event_name":"PostToolUse","tool_name":"Read","tool_input":{"file_path":"e:\\workstuff\\platform_ai_assistant.worktrees\\agents-architectural-review-project-files\\app\\services\\llm_service.py"},"tool_response":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"e:\\workstuff\\platform_ai_assistant.worktrees\\agents-architectural-review-project-files\\app\\services\\llm_service.py","content":"from __future__ import annotations\n\nimport httpx\nimport os\nfrom typing import Optional\nfrom dotenv import load_dotenv\n\nfrom app.services.prompt_builder import build_system_prompt\n\nload_dotenv()\n\nLLM_PROVIDER = os.getenv(\"LLM_PROVIDER\", \"openai\")\nOLLAMA_BASE_URL = os.getenv(\"OLLAMA_BASE_URL\", \"http://localhost:11434\")\nOLLAMA_MODEL = os.getenv(\"OLLAMA_MODEL\", \"llama3.2\")\nOPENAI_API_KEY = os.getenv(\"OPENAI_API_KEY\", \"\")\nOPENAI_MODEL = os.getenv(\"OPENAI_MODEL\", \"gpt-4.1-nano\")\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Public interface\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nasync def ask_llm(\n    question: str,\n    context: str,\n    page: Optional[str] = None,\n    language: str = \"ru\",\n    history: str = \"\",\n    intent: Optional[str] = None,\n    entity: Optional[str] = None,\n    current_step: Optional[int] = None,\n    situation: Optional[str] = None,\n) -> str:\n    system = build_system_prompt(\n        language=language,\n        history=history,\n        intent=intent,\n        entity=entity,\n        current_step=current_step,\n        page=page,\n        situation=situation,\n    )\n\n    # When RAG returns nothing (empty or fallback placeholder), tell the LLM\n    # explicitly so it applies rule 6 (3-tier: allowed topics / grey zone / offtopic)\n    # instead of hallucinating or defaulting to the greeting script from <role>.\n    _EMPTY_SIGNALS = {\"\", \"Контекст недоступен.\", \"Контекст недоступен\"}\n    if not context or context.strip() in _EMPTY_SIGNALS:\n        context_block = (\n            \"<context>\\n\"\n            \"[КОНТЕКСТ ПУСТОЙ — в базе знаний iSEL информации по данному вопросу нет.\\n\"\n            \"Классифицируй вопрос по правилу 6 (уровни A / B / C) и отвечай соответственно.\\n\"\n            \"НЕ выдавай шаблонное приветствие и НЕ игнорируй суть вопроса.]\\n\"\n            \"</context>\"\n        )\n    else:\n        context_block = f\"<context>\\n{context}\\n</context>\"\n\n    prompt = f\"{context_block}\\n\\n<question>\\n{question}\\n</question>\\n\\n<answer>\"\n\n    if LLM_PROVIDER == \"openai\":\n        return await _call_openai(system, prompt)\n    return await _call_ollama(system, prompt)\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Provider implementations\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nasync def _call_openai(system: str, prompt: str) -> str:\n    # timeout=90s: reasoning models (gpt-5-mini, o-series) take up to 60s to produce output.\n    # temperature=1: required by reasoning models — they reject temperature != 1.\n    # max_completion_tokens=8000: reasoning models consume 3000-5000 internal tokens before\n    # visible output; 8000 leaves enough budget for the actual answer.\n    async with httpx.AsyncClient(timeout=90.0) as client:\n        try:\n            response = await client.post(\n                \"https://api.openai.com/v1/chat/completions\",\n                headers={\n                    \"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {OPENAI_API_KEY}\",\n                    \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\",\n                },\n                json={\n                    \"model\": OPENAI_MODEL,\n                    \"messages\": [\n                        {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": system},\n                        {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": prompt},\n                    ],\n                    \"temperature\": 1,\n                    \"max_completion_tokens\": 8000,\n                },\n            )\n            data = response.json()\n            if response.status_code != 200:\n                error_msg = data.get(\"error\", {}).get(\"message\", \"Unknown error\")\n                return f\"Ошибка OpenAI: {error_msg}\"\n            return data[\"choices\"][0][\"message\"][\"content\"]\n        except Exception as e:\n            return f\"Ошибка LLM-сервиса: {str(e)}\"\n\n\nasync def _call_ollama(system: str, prompt: str) -> str:\n    async with httpx.AsyncClient(timeout=180.0) as client:\n        try:\n            response = await client.post(\n                f\"{OLLAMA_BASE_URL}/api/generate\",\n                json={\n                    \"model\": OLLAMA_MODEL,\n                    \"prompt\": prompt,\n                    \"system\": system,\n                    \"stream\": False,\n                    \"options\": {\"temperature\": 0.0},\n                },\n            )\n            data = response.json()\n            return data.get(\"response\", \"Ошибка генерации.\")\n        except Exception as e:\n            return f\"Ошибка LLM-сервиса: {str(e)}\"","numLines":118,"startLine":1,"totalLines":118}},"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VSAF5bg2WE1PVLNFNmpDna","duration_ms":2}

2026-05-25T10:33:59.552Z {"session_id":"89bec47a-fde9-463a-861e-f47ff075ce36","transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\yasmi\\.claude\\projects\\e--workstuff-platform-ai-assistant-worktrees-agents-architectural-review-project-files\\89bec47a-fde9-463a-861e-f47ff075ce36.jsonl","cwd":"e:\\workstuff\\platform_ai_assistant.worktrees\\agents-architectural-review-project-files","permission_mode":"default","effort":{"level":"high"},"hook_event_name":"Stop","stop_hook_active":false,"last_assistant_message":"Теперь у меня полная картина. Вот полный анализ:\n\n---\n\n## Анализ расхождений: ТЗ vs. реальный код\n\n---\n\n### 🔴 БАГИ — реальные ошибки в логике\n\n---\n\n**БАГ #1 — `LinearFlow.MAX_STEPS` захардкожен, `services.yaml` игнорируется**\n\n[linear.py:9](app/flows/linear.py#L9)\n```python\nMAX_STEPS = 5  # захардкожен, не читается из services.yaml\n```\n`primary_connection_residential` имеет `max_steps: 4` в YAML — но `LinearFlow` всегда ограничивает 5 шагами. Бот позволит пользователю \"дойти до шага 5\" там, где его нет. Нужно читать `max_steps` из `ServiceRegistry` при инициализации потока.\n\n---\n\n**БАГ #2 — Новые LinearFlow-сервисы никогда не блокируются (`locked` остаётся `False`)**\n\n[chat.py:404-409](app/routers/chat.py#L404)\n```python\n_can_lock = (\n    (state.intent == \"tu_application\" and ...)\n    or (state.intent == \"real_estate\" and ...)\n)\n# primary_connection_residential и primary_connection_nonresidential — не покрыты!\n```\nСледствие: если пользователь начал заполнять форму первичного подключения (шаг 1+), любое сообщение с ключевым словом другого сервиса переключит интент. FAQ interruption gate тоже не сработает, т.к. проверяет `state.locked`.\n\n---\n\n**БАГ #3 — Rate limit срабатывает ДО rule_based (приветствия расходуют лимит)**\n\n[chat.py:256-269](app/routers/chat.py#L256)\n```python\nif not chat_limiter.is_allowed(request.session_id):  # ← строка 256\n    ...\n# ...\nrule_answer, _ = check_rule(request.message)          # ← строка 266\n```\nТЗ §8.1 утверждает: _\"rate_limit проверяется ПОСЛЕ rule_based — приветствия не расходуют лимит\"_. В коде — наоборот. Реальное поведение: `\"привет\"` засчитывается в счётчик 10 запросов/мин.\n\n---\n\n**БАГ #4 — `source=\"faq_interruption\"` никогда не возвращается клиенту**\n\nТЗ §3.1: `source: \"rule_based\" | \"faq_interruption\" | \"llm\"`\n\nРеальный код — все FAQ interruption и navigation shortcut возвращают `source=\"llm\"`:\n```python\nreturn ChatResponse(answer=nav_answer, source=\"llm\", handoff=False)  # строка 308\nreturn ChatResponse(answer=answer, source=\"llm\", handoff=False)       # строка 355\n```\n`\"faq_interruption\"` используется только в `log_chat_request()` (внутреннее логирование), но не в `ChatResponse`.\n\n---\n\n**БАГ #5 — `handoff` из `check_rule()` всегда игнорируется**\n\n[chat.py:266](app/routers/chat.py#L266)\n```python\nrule_answer, _ = check_rule(request.message)  # handoff отброшен через _\n```\nВ `SYSTEM_COMMANDS` и `NAVIGATION_RULES` у каждой записи есть `\"handoff\": bool` — но это значение никогда не доходит до `ChatResponse`. Все rule_based ответы возвращают `handoff=False` принудительно.\n\n---\n\n**БАГ #6 — `_EMPTY_SIGNALS` создаётся заново при каждом вызове `ask_llm()`**\n\n[llm_service.py:47](app/services/llm_service.py#L47)\n```python\nasync def ask_llm(...):\n    ...\n    _EMPTY_SIGNALS = {\"\", \"Контекст недоступен.\", \"Контекст недоступен\"}  # внутри функции!\n```\n`frozenset` должен быть на уровне модуля — создание объекта при каждом запросе избыточно.\n\n---\n\n### 🟡 РАСХОЖДЕНИЯ — документация не соответствует коду\n\n---\n\n**#7 — LLM-модель для ответов**\n> ТЗ §1.2 / §2.1: `gpt-4.1-nano`\n> `.env`: `OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-5-mini`\n\n---\n\n**#8 — Количество правил в `<rules>`**\n> ТЗ §4.1: \"17 правил генерации ответа\"\n> Факт: 18 правил (добавлено правило о текстовом чате)\n\n---\n\n**#9 — SSE-формат событий `/reindex` полностью отличается**\n\nТЗ §5.2 описывает:\n```\nevent: log    → {\"msg\": \"...\"}\nevent: progress → {\"current\": N, \"total\": M, \"filename\": \"...\"}\nevent: done   → {\"msg\": \"...\", \"total\": M, \"ok\": N, \"failed\": K}\n```\nРеальный [documents.py](app/routers/documents.py):\n```\n{\"status\": \"wiping\"}\n{\"status\": \"init\"}\n{\"status\": \"progress\", \"file\": \"...\", \"done\": N, \"total\": M}\n{\"status\": \"file_error\", \"file\": \"...\", \"error\": \"...\"}\n{\"status\": \"done\", \"total\": N}\n```\n\n---\n\n**#10 — `test_quality_gates.py` в таблице тестов**\n> ТЗ §8.3: файл присутствует в списке\n> Факт: файл удалён, актуальных файлов 7\n\n---\n\n**#11 — Pass rate тестов**\n> ТЗ §8.3: \"~95%\"\n> Факт: 299/299, 100%\n\n---\n\n**#12 — §6.4 \"Добавить keywords в `INTENT_KEYWORDS` в `registry.py`\"**\n`INTENT_KEYWORDS` больше не хардкодится — он строится динамически из YAML:\n```python\nINTENT_KEYWORDS = _registry.build_intent_keywords_map()\n```\nИнструкция в ТЗ ведёт разработчика не туда. Нужно: добавить в `keywords.yaml`.\n\n---\n\n**#13 — `LinearFlow.requires_entity = True` захардкожен, но не используется**\n\n[linear.py:42](app/flows/linear.py#L42): `requires_entity = True` — атрибут класса.\nФактически gate читается только через `_needs_entity_clarification()` в `chat.py`, которая напрямую проверяет `intent == \"tu_application\"`, а не `flow.requires_entity`. Поле в классе декоративное.\n\n---\n\n**#14 — Два независимых детектора шагов могут давать разные результаты**\n\n- `_extract_step_jump()` в [linear.py](app/flows/linear.py#L29) — строгий regex, только \"чистая\" ссылка на шаг\n- `_extract_step_number()` в [chat.py](app/routers/chat.py#L217) — мягкий regex, находит шаг внутри фразы\n\nОба используются в одном пайплайне. Например, \"объясни шаг 2\" — `_extract_step_number` вернёт `2`, а `_extract_step_jump` — `None`. В некоторых контекстах это расхождение логично, но не задокументировано.\n\n---\n\n### Итоговая таблица\n\n| # | Тип | Место | Критичность |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Баг | `linear.py` MAX_STEPS | Высокая — лишний шаг для primary_connection |\n| 2 | Баг | `chat.py` _can_lock | Высокая — новые сервисы не блокируются |\n| 3 | Баг | `chat.py` rate_limit порядок | Средняя — приветствия расходуют лимит |\n| 4 | Расхождение | `chat.py` source | Средняя — фронтенд не видит faq_interruption |\n| 5 | Баг | `chat.py` handoff игнор | Низкая — handoff никогда не передаётся |\n| 6 | Code smell | `llm_service.py` | Низкая — frozenset внутри функции |\n| 7 | Документация | ТЗ §1.2, §2.1 | LLM модель |\n| 8 | Документация | ТЗ §4.1 | Кол-во правил |\n| 9 | Документация | ТЗ §5.2 | SSE формат |\n| 10-14 | Документация | Разные разделы | Минорные |\n\n**Хочешь, исправлю баги #1, #2, #3 (наиболее критичные)?**","background_tasks":[],"session_crons":[]}

